1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:37,809 --> 00:00:39,811
It might have been a memory, not a dream.

3
00:00:43,606 --> 00:00:45,483
If Jang Tae-ha's really a gangster,

4
00:00:46,901 --> 00:00:48,361
this might also

5
00:00:49,028 --> 00:00:51,322
have something to do with him.

6
00:00:53,158 --> 00:00:56,619
Isn't it enough you've ruined your life
with violence already?

7
00:00:56,703 --> 00:01:00,623
Now you want to drag Pil-seung
into that fiery hell with you?

8
00:01:00,707 --> 00:01:01,749
Not my boy.

9
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:03,459
I won't let you!

10
00:01:03,543 --> 00:01:04,627
Mrs. Pang!

11
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,672
No matter how angry you are,

12
00:01:08,756 --> 00:01:11,551
there are things you just don't say.

13
00:01:12,302 --> 00:01:13,386
Everything else aside,

14
00:01:13,469 --> 00:01:16,556
how can you do this when you know
why Tae-ha went down that path?

15
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:21,394
I also won't stand by
and watch my boy get hurt.

16
00:01:22,604 --> 00:01:25,565
I'm sorry we didn't tell you sooner
about Pil-seung,

17
00:01:25,648 --> 00:01:28,651
but if you want to blame or sue anyone,
blame me, the head coach.

18
00:01:29,277 --> 00:01:31,738
Don't take it out on Tae-ha!

19
00:01:38,286 --> 00:01:39,120
You're right.

20
00:01:39,621 --> 00:01:42,373
I went too far.

21
00:01:42,457 --> 00:01:46,502
It's not that I don't know
what you've been through.

22
00:01:46,586 --> 00:01:49,214
I just lost my temper
out of concern for my boy.

23
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:52,342
And I know that not all boxers
become gangsters,

24
00:01:52,425 --> 00:01:55,553
but it's easier to fall in with those guys
than other jobs.

25
00:01:55,637 --> 00:02:00,808
I was scared that those punks
might start eyeing my kid.

26
00:02:01,517 --> 00:02:04,312
What kind of mother would want that?

27
00:02:04,395 --> 00:02:08,608
Please try to understand me, Tae-ha.

28
00:02:12,695 --> 00:02:14,030
Let's go. Come on.

29
00:02:14,113 --> 00:02:15,031
Wait, Mom.

30
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:16,157
Oh, shut it.

31
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:17,700
Mom, please.

32
00:02:43,476 --> 00:02:44,519
Ms. Go.

33
00:02:48,106 --> 00:02:48,940
Ms. Go.

34
00:02:49,023 --> 00:02:50,817
Whoa! Hey, what?

35
00:02:54,195 --> 00:02:55,738
You scared me.

36
00:02:55,822 --> 00:02:57,240
Didn't you see me?

37
00:03:03,663 --> 00:03:04,664
Are you okay?

38
00:03:17,635 --> 00:03:18,553
Are you…

39
00:03:21,014 --> 00:03:21,889
okay?

40
00:03:23,891 --> 00:03:27,103
You know I can take a hit.
I'm just worried about Pil-seung.

41
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,732
What, you think he goes down easy?

42
00:03:31,441 --> 00:03:35,570
He's probably butting heads with his mom,
going a few rounds.

43
00:03:42,577 --> 00:03:43,411
Fancy a drink?

44
00:03:52,170 --> 00:03:53,004
I should go home.

45
00:03:56,007 --> 00:03:56,841
All right.

46
00:03:57,675 --> 00:04:01,137
It's a good thing you have someone at home
on a day like this.

47
00:04:02,096 --> 00:04:03,806
The warmth of someone being home.

48
00:04:04,849 --> 00:04:06,225
It makes a difference.

49
00:04:08,811 --> 00:04:09,645
I'll get going.

50
00:04:19,113 --> 00:04:22,158
This morning, the ceremony
for the Irang-dong development project

51
00:04:22,241 --> 00:04:26,954
was attended by Gangju City officials
and Mirae Eden Company representatives.

52
00:04:27,455 --> 00:04:31,501
This project is a joint effort between
Gangju City and Mirae Eden Company,

53
00:04:31,584 --> 00:04:36,130
and the plan is to complete
the development in three phases by 2029.

54
00:04:36,631 --> 00:04:39,634
Though the blueprint for this project
was presented in 2020,

55
00:04:39,717 --> 00:04:43,846
it was effectively halted
due to the real estate market downturn.

56
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:46,224
But earlier this year,
the development area was…

57
00:04:46,307 --> 00:04:47,558
Go Eun-sae.

58
00:04:51,479 --> 00:04:54,107
Drink this. It'll help you calm down.

59
00:05:03,825 --> 00:05:05,868
Do you still not believe Tae-ha?

60
00:05:17,755 --> 00:05:19,006
I believed him

61
00:05:20,341 --> 00:05:21,300
a little bit.

62
00:05:23,970 --> 00:05:26,389
In the midst of this absurd situation,

63
00:05:26,472 --> 00:05:27,682
there were moments

64
00:05:28,391 --> 00:05:30,726
when he seemed sincere.

65
00:05:31,644 --> 00:05:33,271
Sorry I don't express myself well.

66
00:05:33,855 --> 00:05:36,274
You're the only woman I've ever liked,

67
00:05:37,692 --> 00:05:40,027
so I don't really know how.

68
00:05:41,612 --> 00:05:44,073
He wasn't exactly my ideal type,

69
00:05:44,991 --> 00:05:47,869
but he didn't seem like
a bad person either.

70
00:05:47,952 --> 00:05:50,163
I never knew she was so pretty.

71
00:05:57,295 --> 00:05:59,672
But it turns out he's a gangster.

72
00:06:00,381 --> 00:06:03,134
And everything he said to me was a lie.

73
00:06:03,634 --> 00:06:06,512
Apparently, my name isn't even Go Eun-sae.

74
00:06:06,596 --> 00:06:07,638
It's Go Ji-won.

75
00:06:08,222 --> 00:06:09,056
Sorry?

76
00:06:12,768 --> 00:06:15,146
I don't know where to start
questioning things again,

77
00:06:15,229 --> 00:06:18,024
or why Jang Tae-ha lied to me
about all of this,

78
00:06:18,524 --> 00:06:20,568
and what I'm supposed to do now.

79
00:06:22,278 --> 00:06:23,779
I don't know anything anymore.

80
00:06:28,784 --> 00:06:29,952
I'm scared.

81
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:34,332
Go Eun-sae!

82
00:06:37,585 --> 00:06:38,878
Go Eun-sae!

83
00:06:40,379 --> 00:06:41,464
Eun-sae…

84
00:06:48,804 --> 00:06:49,722
Hello?

85
00:06:49,805 --> 00:06:51,140
It's me, Min Su-ji.

86
00:06:53,518 --> 00:06:56,187
Right. I can't really talk right now…

87
00:06:56,270 --> 00:06:57,563
Are you looking for Ms. Go?

88
00:07:10,409 --> 00:07:11,327
Is she here?

89
00:07:12,245 --> 00:07:13,079
Yes.

90
00:07:13,579 --> 00:07:17,500
I heard her telling Gi-jun
that she found out you're a gangster.

91
00:07:18,292 --> 00:07:21,295
And that her name is Go Ji-won,
not Go Eun-sae.

92
00:07:21,379 --> 00:07:23,589
She said she saw
her friend's social media.

93
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,801
What's going on?

94
00:07:27,301 --> 00:07:30,805
Is she really your girlfriend?

95
00:07:31,889 --> 00:07:33,015
Now, then…

96
00:07:35,268 --> 00:07:37,436
-What should we do?
-Sorry?

97
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,398
I understand your situation,
but that doesn't mean…

98
00:07:40,481 --> 00:07:43,693
I can't exactly let you crash at my place.

99
00:07:43,776 --> 00:07:48,030
And I can't lend you money for a place
to stay, since you can't pay me back.

100
00:07:48,531 --> 00:07:49,365
Doctor.

101
00:07:49,448 --> 00:07:50,533
Yes?

102
00:07:50,616 --> 00:07:52,076
You don't have many

103
00:07:53,077 --> 00:07:54,745
friends, do you?

104
00:07:54,829 --> 00:07:56,414
No, I guess I don't.

105
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:02,628
I was just joking to cheer you up.
Come on.

106
00:08:02,712 --> 00:08:03,963
You were being serious.

107
00:08:06,674 --> 00:08:08,175
Well, I'm sorry.

108
00:08:12,722 --> 00:08:13,848
Jang Tae-ha.

109
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:20,313
I'll explain everything, so let's go home.

110
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:23,107
How can I trust a thug and go with him?

111
00:08:26,611 --> 00:08:28,738
You should trust what you've experienced.

112
00:08:29,488 --> 00:08:31,115
Has he ever been a threat to you?

113
00:08:32,199 --> 00:08:34,994
Has he ever threatened you,
used violence, or extorted you?

114
00:08:37,455 --> 00:08:40,333
If not, then Tae-ha isn't a thug to you.

115
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:41,751
He's just

116
00:08:42,627 --> 00:08:44,211
an ordinary man, isn't he?

117
00:08:57,516 --> 00:08:58,434
Let's talk outside.

118
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,294
-Go Eun-sae.
-But I'm not Go Eun-sae.

119
00:09:25,378 --> 00:09:26,545
I'm Go Ji-won, aren't I?

120
00:09:26,629 --> 00:09:29,965
Go Ji-won is your legal name.
Eun-sae is the name your mother gave you.

121
00:09:31,759 --> 00:09:34,553
Are you getting caught up
in your own lies? My mother?

122
00:09:34,637 --> 00:09:36,013
You said I was an orphan.

123
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:39,433
Your mother left you at an orphanage
right after you were born.

124
00:09:39,517 --> 00:09:41,227
The orphanage head only realized

125
00:09:41,727 --> 00:09:44,563
after registering your birth
under the name Go Ji-won

126
00:09:45,481 --> 00:09:48,442
that your name was Go Eun-sae
in your mother's maternity notebook.

127
00:09:49,485 --> 00:09:52,279
You liked the name Go Eun-sae better.

128
00:09:53,948 --> 00:09:55,908
You said she wouldn't have given

129
00:09:55,991 --> 00:09:58,452
such a pretty name
to a baby she didn't love.

130
00:09:59,787 --> 00:10:01,872
You didn't even resent her
for abandoning you.

131
00:10:17,555 --> 00:10:20,433
And the designer goods?
I saw pictures of me and my friend.

132
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:22,810
I was dressed from head to toe
in designer items.

133
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:26,731
Then why don't I have anything like that
in my closet or shoe rack?

134
00:10:27,648 --> 00:10:29,275
You got rid of them when we moved.

135
00:10:29,358 --> 00:10:31,068
-Why?
-I never asked why.

136
00:10:41,579 --> 00:10:42,747
I…

137
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:51,172
I'm sorry that I was…

138
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:55,885
a gangster.

139
00:10:58,637 --> 00:11:00,514
I was too ashamed to tell you.

140
00:11:03,726 --> 00:11:07,688
If I'd known you were a thug,
I wouldn't have believed a word you said.

141
00:11:08,731 --> 00:11:10,149
If I know anything,

142
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:14,779
it's that I'd never,
not in this life or any other,

143
00:11:14,862 --> 00:11:17,573
fall for some lowlife gangster.

144
00:11:21,494 --> 00:11:22,828
I don't do that anymore.

145
00:11:22,912 --> 00:11:25,498
I won't ever use my fists
outside the ring anymore.

146
00:11:26,624 --> 00:11:27,666
I promise.

147
00:11:27,750 --> 00:11:29,126
No, forget it.

148
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:32,838
Just why are you putting on this act
to keep me here?

149
00:11:32,922 --> 00:11:35,549
What in the world do you want from me?

150
00:11:37,468 --> 00:11:38,302
Nothing else.

151
00:11:40,346 --> 00:11:42,223
Just don't disappear without a word.

152
00:11:44,016 --> 00:11:45,184
Just stay out of danger.

153
00:11:45,684 --> 00:11:47,019
Just…

154
00:11:48,896 --> 00:11:50,356
Just stay safe.

155
00:11:56,779 --> 00:11:58,072
Why are you overreacting?

156
00:11:58,155 --> 00:12:01,367
How would you know
if he's really Ms. Go's boyfriend?

157
00:12:03,369 --> 00:12:04,703
He is her boyfriend.

158
00:12:04,787 --> 00:12:07,998
Is she really your girlfriend?

159
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:10,334
Is Eun-sae okay?

160
00:12:11,502 --> 00:12:13,128
-What?
-Has she been crying?

161
00:12:13,629 --> 00:12:14,463
Is she hurt?

162
00:12:26,267 --> 00:12:27,101
Go inside.

163
00:12:27,685 --> 00:12:29,019
Ms. Go is fine.

164
00:12:32,523 --> 00:12:36,277
Do you remember when we went to Yeosu,
and I left the hotel after we argued?

165
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,987
Why are you bringing that up now?

166
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,573
Was it right to ghost me for hours
because you were mad?

167
00:12:40,656 --> 00:12:41,740
I got lost back then.

168
00:12:42,741 --> 00:12:46,537
I was just gonna cool off, then go back,
but you know I get lost easily.

169
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:50,624
I was in an unfamiliar city,
and I'd left my phone behind.

170
00:12:51,125 --> 00:12:52,918
I was terrified.

171
00:12:53,002 --> 00:12:55,713
When I got back to the hotel
after wandering for hours,

172
00:12:55,796 --> 00:12:59,508
you asked if I was happy I'd win
by making you worry.

173
00:13:04,138 --> 00:13:06,891
Perhaps the one
who was never really a boyfriend

174
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:09,101
isn't Tae-ha,

175
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:11,270
but you.

176
00:13:50,893 --> 00:13:52,478
PARK HYO-JIN
HYOGENIE_1227

177
00:13:52,561 --> 00:13:54,730
HI. THIS IS JI-WON.
YOU'RE MY FRIEND, HYO-JIN, RIGHT?

178
00:13:54,813 --> 00:13:56,357
Please read it.

179
00:13:57,608 --> 00:13:59,777
Please read it and get back to me.

180
00:14:08,994 --> 00:14:12,539
Hey, hey, don't run

181
00:14:12,623 --> 00:14:16,669
You'll only get hungrier

182
00:14:17,503 --> 00:14:21,632
This heart-aching road of the barley hump…

183
00:14:21,715 --> 00:14:23,384
Hey there, Song-wol.

184
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:25,344
These are dried persimmons.

185
00:14:25,427 --> 00:14:28,347
Put them in the freezer
and eat them with your grandma.

186
00:14:31,016 --> 00:14:35,896
How did you ever live through those days?

187
00:14:37,523 --> 00:14:41,193
Mother's sorrow

188
00:14:41,276 --> 00:14:46,198
Endless days of living on roots and bark

189
00:14:46,782 --> 00:14:52,329
-Have you been well, ma'am?
-As those times fade into the wind

190
00:14:52,413 --> 00:14:56,417
-I haven't been able to visit you lately.
-Mother's sorrow, buried…

191
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:59,378
Are you happy that Tae-ha moved down here?

192
00:15:01,714 --> 00:15:02,548
Yes, ma'am.

193
00:15:07,177 --> 00:15:10,014
I'm so sorry.

194
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:14,810
I said something
I shouldn't have to Tae-ha.

195
00:15:17,855 --> 00:15:19,857
Despite knowing why he ended up like that

196
00:15:20,858 --> 00:15:24,528
and everything you went through
to raise him,

197
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,323
I was blinded by my love for my own child.

198
00:15:29,408 --> 00:15:31,827
So I drove a nail

199
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:34,747
into poor Tae-ha's heart.

200
00:15:42,004 --> 00:15:45,215
Even though I have two children of my own,

201
00:15:45,716 --> 00:15:48,677
and I've grown older,

202
00:15:50,304 --> 00:15:51,847
I still have a long way to go…

203
00:15:53,974 --> 00:15:56,477
before I can call myself a true adult.

204
00:16:02,941 --> 00:16:06,487
I'll make sure to prepare
the grandest of celebrations

205
00:16:06,987 --> 00:16:08,906
for your 80th birthday.

206
00:16:09,698 --> 00:16:15,079
I know that couldn't possibly
make up for my mistake, but still.

207
00:16:16,246 --> 00:16:18,916
Please go… a little easy on me.

208
00:16:27,132 --> 00:16:31,261
You're telling me to stop whining
and shut up, right?

209
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:36,892
Please stay with us for a long time.

210
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:40,479
Until this fool, Pang Hui-ja,
finally grows up.

211
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:06,088
It's me, Hyo-jin.

212
00:17:07,422 --> 00:17:09,383
I'm texting after seeing your DM.

213
00:17:09,466 --> 00:17:10,634
Let's meet.

214
00:17:13,137 --> 00:17:15,556
It's okay now. I'm okay.

215
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,373
HONG DO-YEOP

216
00:17:42,207 --> 00:17:43,292
Hi, Coach.

217
00:17:46,086 --> 00:17:47,129
Who's here?

218
00:17:51,091 --> 00:17:52,176
Something's come up.

219
00:17:53,093 --> 00:17:55,137
These are Grandma's favorite playlists.

220
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:57,097
Give them to Mrs. Pang at the party.

221
00:17:58,015 --> 00:17:59,057
What?

222
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:01,435
Her only grandson is skipping her party?

223
00:18:03,812 --> 00:18:05,606
She'll need these, so make sure you go.

224
00:18:06,106 --> 00:18:07,566
Go there and stay put.

225
00:18:13,113 --> 00:18:14,239
What's with him?

226
00:18:15,574 --> 00:18:17,576
What's more important than his grandma?

227
00:18:36,136 --> 00:18:37,137
Sir!

228
00:18:37,888 --> 00:18:39,348
It's me, Gang-rok!

229
00:18:39,431 --> 00:18:40,766
Have you been well?

230
00:19:07,584 --> 00:19:10,629
Sir, they sliced my Achilles' heel.

231
00:19:10,712 --> 00:19:12,631
If you leave, they usually cut off both,

232
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:16,218
but I'm such a small fry
that they let me off with one.

233
00:19:19,930 --> 00:19:22,474
You were like a father to me.

234
00:19:22,557 --> 00:19:25,727
Why would I stay in Eden
when my dad's not there?

235
00:19:28,855 --> 00:19:29,815
How did you find me?

236
00:19:29,898 --> 00:19:32,526
Ages ago, we drank together,
just the two of us.

237
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:35,821
You got drunk
and told me about your hometown.

238
00:19:35,904 --> 00:19:39,408
You said you wanted to go back
to the boxing gym there when you retired.

239
00:19:39,491 --> 00:19:42,327
I looked it up,
and there's only one boxing gym in Gujin.

240
00:19:48,292 --> 00:19:49,626
I must ask…

241
00:19:52,254 --> 00:19:53,171
Sir,

242
00:19:54,423 --> 00:19:55,841
did you save Prosecutor Go?

243
00:20:01,638 --> 00:20:03,056
I saw her earlier,

244
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,017
very much alive.

245
00:20:09,896 --> 00:20:11,565
CONGRATULATIONS ON
MS. GO YEON-HONG'S 80TH BIRTHDAY

246
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:16,528
Nice!

247
00:20:22,284 --> 00:20:24,077
Here.

248
00:20:24,161 --> 00:20:25,287
There you go.

249
00:20:25,370 --> 00:20:27,622
All right, here goes!

250
00:20:27,706 --> 00:20:31,084
I was told to give this to Mrs. Pang.

251
00:20:31,168 --> 00:20:33,462
They're songs Grandma likes.

252
00:20:34,004 --> 00:20:36,131
I'll get going, then.

253
00:20:36,214 --> 00:20:37,507
Hang on, lady.

254
00:20:37,591 --> 00:20:39,926
Where are you going? Eat before you go.

255
00:20:40,802 --> 00:20:41,636
It's okay.

256
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:42,846
Hold on.

257
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:46,683
Aren't you her granddaughter-in-law?

258
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:49,353
First, you show up fashionably late.

259
00:20:49,436 --> 00:20:52,522
And now what?
You're gonna show your face and leave?

260
00:20:53,899 --> 00:20:55,817
I'm not her granddaughter-in-law.

261
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:58,612
Sure, you haven't had a wedding yet,

262
00:20:58,695 --> 00:21:01,782
but you're practically her family.

263
00:21:04,117 --> 00:21:05,619
-I'll get going.
-What?

264
00:21:06,203 --> 00:21:09,039
-I said eat before you go.
-I said I don't want to.

265
00:21:09,623 --> 00:21:13,960
You shouldn't go on an empty stomach.
At least eat this before you go.

266
00:21:14,878 --> 00:21:15,921
Oh my!

267
00:21:22,135 --> 00:21:23,011
Go Ji-won!

268
00:21:23,095 --> 00:21:26,014
I said I'll make you eat gochujang
if you leave food, didn't I?

269
00:21:26,098 --> 00:21:27,057
Eat it!

270
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:29,768
Eat! I said eat!

271
00:21:29,851 --> 00:21:31,103
Open!

272
00:21:31,186 --> 00:21:33,397
Open your mouth! Wide!

273
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,356
Open!

274
00:21:35,732 --> 00:21:38,360
Have you lost all your manners?

275
00:21:39,069 --> 00:21:42,697
Hey, you can make a scene,
but there are lines you don't cross.

276
00:21:42,781 --> 00:21:45,492
She did that so you wouldn't go hungry.

277
00:21:46,952 --> 00:21:50,080
Yeah, but… did I ever say I was hungry?

278
00:21:50,163 --> 00:21:51,873
Did I say I wanted to eat?

279
00:21:52,666 --> 00:21:56,044
People in the countryside might think
that's how you show affection,

280
00:21:56,128 --> 00:21:58,213
but it's only affection if it's welcome.

281
00:21:58,296 --> 00:22:01,258
Forcing food on someone
who doesn't want to eat

282
00:22:01,883 --> 00:22:03,760
is torture.

283
00:22:03,844 --> 00:22:05,345
What? Torture?

284
00:22:06,721 --> 00:22:08,765
Hey, don't you have parents?

285
00:22:09,558 --> 00:22:12,310
Didn't your parents teach you
to be respectful?

286
00:22:14,229 --> 00:22:15,105
No.

287
00:22:15,939 --> 00:22:19,192
Apparently, I don't have any parents
and grew up in an orphanage.

288
00:22:20,318 --> 00:22:22,904
-What's going on?
-What's happening?

289
00:22:23,822 --> 00:22:24,698
What?

290
00:22:24,781 --> 00:22:26,783
But what difference
would parents have made?

291
00:22:27,367 --> 00:22:30,954
You have parents, and I don't,
yet we're being equally disrespectful.

292
00:22:31,705 --> 00:22:35,876
I should seriously knock some sense
into that thick head of yours!

293
00:22:35,959 --> 00:22:39,754
I could also speak rudely to you,
but I'm holding back.

294
00:22:42,632 --> 00:22:45,635
You should know that, at the very least,
compared to everyone here,

295
00:22:46,219 --> 00:22:48,847
I have a certain level of class and grace,

296
00:22:49,389 --> 00:22:50,974
so I'm letting this slide.

297
00:22:52,184 --> 00:22:56,438
So what brings someone of such class
to the countryside?

298
00:22:58,315 --> 00:22:59,774
That's why I'm leaving.

299
00:23:00,525 --> 00:23:03,195
Because I can't bear to stay
in this low-class village

300
00:23:03,695 --> 00:23:05,655
for another day.

301
00:23:07,616 --> 00:23:08,825
-Look at her.
-Ms. Go.

302
00:23:08,909 --> 00:23:11,203
-Let her go.
-That brat! Good heavens.

303
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:15,582
Hui-ja, just let it go.

304
00:23:15,665 --> 00:23:17,042
Just let her go.

305
00:23:17,876 --> 00:23:19,544
Yeah, why wait until tomorrow?

306
00:23:31,348 --> 00:23:32,390
To Seoul, please.

307
00:23:39,105 --> 00:23:41,358
I thought that was just like you, sir.

308
00:23:41,441 --> 00:23:45,612
The man I served all this time
has always been above taking a life.

309
00:23:47,155 --> 00:23:49,950
So does Prosecutor Go live here now?

310
00:23:50,033 --> 00:23:53,537
Has she given up being a prosecutor?
Is it to stay off the chairman's radar?

311
00:23:55,121 --> 00:23:57,165
-Gang-rok.
-Yes, sir?

312
00:23:58,542 --> 00:23:59,960
Why are you here?

313
00:24:04,548 --> 00:24:06,383
I want to live here too.

314
00:24:06,466 --> 00:24:09,135
I don't care what we do.
I just want to be with you.

315
00:24:09,219 --> 00:24:10,762
Please take me in.

316
00:24:33,159 --> 00:24:34,995
There's something you don't know.

317
00:24:36,496 --> 00:24:37,330
Sorry?

318
00:24:37,414 --> 00:24:39,583
Taking someone's life

319
00:24:41,293 --> 00:24:42,419
is not beneath me.

320
00:24:47,924 --> 00:24:49,843
When it comes to protecting my people,

321
00:24:50,427 --> 00:24:51,595
nothing's beneath me.

322
00:24:53,805 --> 00:24:57,100
That means that if you came here
with a hidden agenda…

323
00:25:00,478 --> 00:25:02,230
I will kill you.

324
00:25:05,191 --> 00:25:06,359
I don't have one.

325
00:25:07,485 --> 00:25:08,612
Please believe me.

326
00:25:19,748 --> 00:25:21,875
DO JEONG-HWA

327
00:25:23,752 --> 00:25:24,586
Hello.

328
00:25:29,257 --> 00:25:30,091
I'm sorry?

329
00:25:53,406 --> 00:25:54,991
I should've done this sooner.

330
00:25:56,618 --> 00:25:58,953
Now I can breathe.

331
00:26:01,915 --> 00:26:03,583
Just don't disappear without a word.

332
00:26:05,085 --> 00:26:06,628
Just stay out of danger.

333
00:26:10,632 --> 00:26:11,925
No.

334
00:26:14,260 --> 00:26:15,095
You did well.

335
00:26:16,513 --> 00:26:18,098
It'll all be over tomorrow.

336
00:26:18,973 --> 00:26:19,974
JANG TAE-HA
6 MISSED CALLS

337
00:26:20,058 --> 00:26:22,268
You've held up well all this time.

338
00:26:24,979 --> 00:26:26,398
Go Eun-sae!

339
00:26:28,733 --> 00:26:30,068
Go Eun-sae!

340
00:26:32,445 --> 00:26:33,822
Go Eun-sae!

341
00:26:44,666 --> 00:26:45,917
Eun-sae!

342
00:26:59,556 --> 00:27:00,682
GO EUN-SAE

343
00:27:03,768 --> 00:27:04,686
Go Eun-sae, please.

344
00:27:04,769 --> 00:27:08,440
The phone is turned off.
You will be directed to voicemail.

345
00:27:08,523 --> 00:27:09,691
Please leave a message…

346
00:27:10,275 --> 00:27:11,693
Where the hell did you go?

347
00:27:14,946 --> 00:27:16,197
If it's Seoul…

348
00:27:16,948 --> 00:27:18,241
If you went to Seoul…

349
00:27:21,369 --> 00:27:22,704
No. Please, no.

350
00:28:25,809 --> 00:28:28,353
We have so many eyes in Seoul.

351
00:28:28,978 --> 00:28:29,896
Did you think

352
00:28:31,314 --> 00:28:32,816
you'd go unseen?

353
00:28:40,490 --> 00:28:41,491
Prosecutor.

354
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:52,794
Go Eun-sae!

355
00:29:35,003 --> 00:29:35,920
No!

356
00:30:11,706 --> 00:30:14,125
KIM GANG-ROK

357
00:30:14,626 --> 00:30:17,754
Sir, I thought about it all night.

358
00:30:17,837 --> 00:30:20,632
If Prosecutor Go doesn't have any ID,

359
00:30:20,715 --> 00:30:22,800
whose name did she use
to get a phone number?

360
00:30:22,884 --> 00:30:23,885
Why do you ask?

361
00:30:33,895 --> 00:30:35,313
Today's finally the day.

362
00:30:35,813 --> 00:30:38,358
Now I'll finally find out…

363
00:30:40,526 --> 00:30:41,778
the truth.

364
00:30:59,128 --> 00:30:59,963
Hyo-jin?

365
00:31:01,047 --> 00:31:01,881
Yeah.

366
00:31:05,009 --> 00:31:07,053
It's me, Park Hyo-jin.

367
00:31:10,848 --> 00:31:11,975
Thanks.

368
00:31:21,651 --> 00:31:23,611
So we really are friends.

369
00:31:27,323 --> 00:31:29,367
I finally met my best friend.

370
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:34,372
TO HYO-JIN
FROM EUN-SAE

371
00:31:36,749 --> 00:31:38,001
"Eun-sae"?

372
00:31:40,545 --> 00:31:42,839
Isn't my name Go Ji-won?

373
00:31:42,922 --> 00:31:44,924
That's your legal name.

374
00:31:45,425 --> 00:31:47,343
Go Eun-sae is the name your mom gave you.

375
00:31:47,927 --> 00:31:51,639
You liked that name better,
so I called you Eun-sae sometimes.

376
00:31:52,557 --> 00:31:53,891
Go Ji-won is your legal name.

377
00:31:53,975 --> 00:31:56,144
Eun-sae is the name your mother gave you.

378
00:31:57,895 --> 00:31:59,022
I see.

379
00:32:00,648 --> 00:32:02,400
But do you really

380
00:32:02,984 --> 00:32:04,152
not remember anything?

381
00:32:05,445 --> 00:32:07,739
Yeah. When I opened my eyes,
I was in the hospital.

382
00:32:07,822 --> 00:32:10,324
I couldn't remember a thing.

383
00:32:11,075 --> 00:32:14,746
Then this boxing coach from the country
showed up out of the blue,

384
00:32:14,829 --> 00:32:17,290
saying that we'd been living together
for two years.

385
00:32:17,373 --> 00:32:19,125
That I was an orphan with no family.

386
00:32:20,418 --> 00:32:23,379
It was just impossible to believe.

387
00:32:24,255 --> 00:32:26,591
What did I use to do?

388
00:32:34,140 --> 00:32:35,600
What that man said…

389
00:32:41,022 --> 00:32:41,856
is all true.

390
00:32:44,275 --> 00:32:45,109
What?

391
00:32:45,193 --> 00:32:47,111
You did grow up in an orphanage,

392
00:32:47,195 --> 00:32:49,280
your boyfriend was a boxing coach,

393
00:32:49,363 --> 00:32:51,199
and you didn't have a job as such.

394
00:32:56,537 --> 00:32:59,415
Wait, but that… can't be true.

395
00:32:59,499 --> 00:33:03,086
In all your Instagram photos,
I was dressed in designer clothes.

396
00:33:06,714 --> 00:33:08,508
Who do you think bought that for you?

397
00:33:10,093 --> 00:33:12,303
-What?
-Be good to your boyfriend.

398
00:33:12,386 --> 00:33:14,722
He took care of you despite who you were.

399
00:33:21,729 --> 00:33:22,855
But…

400
00:33:24,565 --> 00:33:25,650
Why…

401
00:33:26,526 --> 00:33:28,986
As my friend, why would you
talk about me like that?

402
00:33:33,866 --> 00:33:35,076
We're friends.

403
00:33:37,078 --> 00:33:37,912
Yeah.

404
00:33:38,913 --> 00:33:40,123
We…

405
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:43,334
used to be.

406
00:33:45,378 --> 00:33:48,005
I'll get you your drink and rice.

407
00:33:48,089 --> 00:33:50,299
-Thanks.
-Can I get you anything else?

408
00:33:50,383 --> 00:33:52,927
-We're good, thanks.
-Enjoy your meal.

409
00:34:03,062 --> 00:34:04,522
-Hey, come here.
-What is it?

410
00:34:04,605 --> 00:34:06,190
Switch shoes with me.

411
00:34:06,274 --> 00:34:07,316
What?

412
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,526
Forget it.

413
00:34:08,609 --> 00:34:10,820
Come on, I want my legs to look longer.

414
00:34:11,654 --> 00:34:13,322
There's a cute customer over there.

415
00:34:13,406 --> 00:34:14,240
Hurry.

416
00:34:15,366 --> 00:34:17,618
-My feet are cold.
-Why are you barefoot?

417
00:34:19,120 --> 00:34:20,872
-Hey, careful.
-I'm okay.

418
00:34:20,955 --> 00:34:22,456
-I'm going.
-Hey.

419
00:34:22,957 --> 00:34:24,792
Go Eun-sae, seriously?

420
00:34:27,044 --> 00:34:30,298
We met in our early twenties
while working part-time.

421
00:34:30,381 --> 00:34:32,383
We clicked and quickly became friends.

422
00:34:33,217 --> 00:34:34,886
Is that right?

423
00:34:35,803 --> 00:34:39,307
You're right. I am in the area, but…

424
00:34:39,807 --> 00:34:40,808
Yes.

425
00:34:42,101 --> 00:34:42,935
No, it's fine.

426
00:34:43,436 --> 00:34:45,688
Yes, understood, sir.

427
00:34:46,939 --> 00:34:51,485
I'm sorry. My boss just called me,
and I think I have to go.

428
00:34:51,569 --> 00:34:52,570
But you just got here.

429
00:34:52,653 --> 00:34:54,572
There's an important drinks thing.

430
00:34:54,655 --> 00:34:58,701
You told me to come no matter what,
so I even closed my nail salon.

431
00:34:58,784 --> 00:35:02,538
Come on, you can't compare
closing your salon to my work drinks.

432
00:35:09,086 --> 00:35:10,880
How much does your salon make in a day?

433
00:35:11,881 --> 00:35:15,551
Let's say it's 70,000 won per appointment.
I'll send you 700,000 won.

434
00:35:16,135 --> 00:35:17,803
-What?
-I'm sorry.

435
00:35:17,887 --> 00:35:18,888
See you!

436
00:35:36,906 --> 00:35:39,200
But at a certain point, you changed.

437
00:35:39,951 --> 00:35:42,995
What? Hyo-jin bought this?

438
00:35:43,579 --> 00:35:46,040
But this costs over five million won.

439
00:35:46,540 --> 00:35:49,335
She said she considered it for months
before buying it.

440
00:35:52,255 --> 00:35:54,090
I guess she'll be back for a refund.

441
00:35:58,302 --> 00:36:00,846
Time and time again, you hurt me.

442
00:36:02,932 --> 00:36:06,143
You often made me feel
miserable and humiliated.

443
00:36:13,317 --> 00:36:14,902
I really did that?

444
00:36:18,698 --> 00:36:21,075
It's not that I wasn't worried
when you went missing,

445
00:36:21,158 --> 00:36:23,536
but knowing that the person
who hurt me was gone

446
00:36:24,328 --> 00:36:25,246
wasn't so bad.

447
00:36:26,455 --> 00:36:30,042
Now that I've seen you're okay,
please don't contact me anymore.

448
00:36:30,751 --> 00:36:32,545
Wait. I'm sorry.

449
00:36:34,297 --> 00:36:37,383
I'm just having a hard time
believing what you're saying right now.

450
00:36:37,466 --> 00:36:40,928
There isn't a single designer item
in the house I live in right now.

451
00:36:41,012 --> 00:36:42,847
How do you explain that?

452
00:36:42,930 --> 00:36:45,641
You're not lying to me, too, are you?

453
00:36:51,480 --> 00:36:52,690
Ji-won.

454
00:36:58,821 --> 00:37:01,991
Isn't it obvious why you wouldn't have
the designer items you bought?

455
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,785
You returned them.

456
00:37:06,203 --> 00:37:07,955
Or sold them because you needed money.

457
00:37:09,832 --> 00:37:10,875
That's why

458
00:37:12,168 --> 00:37:14,628
you should've known
to live within your means.

459
00:37:24,764 --> 00:37:26,015
Wait, I…

460
00:37:44,784 --> 00:37:47,453
SORRY FOR NOT OPENING THE DOOR
WHY AM I ALWAYS SO SORRY?

461
00:37:59,256 --> 00:38:01,509
At the very least,
compared to everyone here,

462
00:38:01,592 --> 00:38:04,512
I have a certain level of class and grace,

463
00:38:05,304 --> 00:38:06,722
so I'm letting this slide.

464
00:38:08,349 --> 00:38:09,934
Class? What class?

465
00:38:10,643 --> 00:38:12,144
I was the lowest of them all.

466
00:38:18,442 --> 00:38:21,987
If the phone is under your name,
can't we track it?

467
00:38:22,071 --> 00:38:26,575
These days, they can track your phone
with your consent if you lose it.

468
00:38:31,914 --> 00:38:33,541
What do I do?

469
00:38:39,130 --> 00:38:41,674
I'm the worst.

470
00:39:03,863 --> 00:39:04,947
Go Eun-sae.

471
00:39:28,304 --> 00:39:30,306
Why are you on the street like this?

472
00:39:30,389 --> 00:39:31,515
What are you doing here?

473
00:39:32,183 --> 00:39:34,059
Forget it. I don't want to talk about it.

474
00:39:39,190 --> 00:39:40,691
Let's just go home.

475
00:39:48,282 --> 00:39:50,534
How could I go back there?

476
00:39:50,618 --> 00:39:54,079
I made a total mess when I left.

477
00:39:54,163 --> 00:39:59,251
I said all kinds of things
to your grandma and the ladies,

478
00:39:59,335 --> 00:40:03,339
yelling like someone
who would never come back.

479
00:40:04,548 --> 00:40:07,092
How could I go back now?

480
00:40:11,347 --> 00:40:13,098
Oh my goodness.

481
00:40:17,061 --> 00:40:21,899
I'm so mad that this is all I amounted to.

482
00:40:58,394 --> 00:40:59,436
Let's eat something.

483
00:41:03,232 --> 00:41:04,358
Hey, Tae-ha.

484
00:41:05,776 --> 00:41:09,905
Does your wife use cement
instead of makeup or something?

485
00:41:10,948 --> 00:41:14,076
It's just that she has such thick skin.

486
00:41:16,412 --> 00:41:18,664
Why are you so silent?

487
00:41:18,747 --> 00:41:25,212
Right. I guess you can't talk to us ladies
who are so far beneath you.

488
00:41:25,296 --> 00:41:26,171
She just--

489
00:41:26,255 --> 00:41:29,216
Come on, you're just as bad.

490
00:41:29,300 --> 00:41:32,344
Think hard about which side to take,
you spineless dummy.

491
00:41:32,428 --> 00:41:35,556
Do you even know
what she did to your grandmother?

492
00:41:36,056 --> 00:41:40,394
If you still have that mouth of yours
that spewed out all those nasty words,

493
00:41:40,477 --> 00:41:41,979
why don't you say something?

494
00:41:42,479 --> 00:41:45,316
After ruining an 80-year-old woman's
birthday party,

495
00:41:45,399 --> 00:41:49,570
how could you have the nerve
to crawl back here?

496
00:41:50,821 --> 00:41:52,448
I told her to come.

497
00:41:57,286 --> 00:41:58,996
You did, ma'am?

498
00:41:59,079 --> 00:42:01,457
Yes, I asked her to come back.

499
00:42:04,168 --> 00:42:05,544
Hey, Song-wol.

500
00:42:05,628 --> 00:42:07,921
She's not in her right mind
right now, is she?

501
00:42:08,505 --> 00:42:09,590
What if I'm not?

502
00:42:09,673 --> 00:42:12,134
Are you going to kick her out?

503
00:42:13,761 --> 00:42:15,179
Of course we wouldn't…

504
00:42:15,262 --> 00:42:18,474
I just asked my family to return.

505
00:42:18,974 --> 00:42:20,809
Do you have a problem with that?

506
00:42:24,438 --> 00:42:27,650
So leave the girl alone now.

507
00:42:28,984 --> 00:42:30,069
Okay?

508
00:43:03,268 --> 00:43:04,687
By any chance,

509
00:43:05,604 --> 00:43:09,316
did you ask your grandma to do that?

510
00:43:10,818 --> 00:43:12,820
How would I know
when she'd come to her senses?

511
00:43:16,323 --> 00:43:17,533
Then why…

512
00:43:20,953 --> 00:43:22,079
Because she's my grandma.

513
00:43:40,472 --> 00:43:44,017
I have to go to the gym real quick.

514
00:43:45,602 --> 00:43:46,687
Okay.

515
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:54,611
I have to… go somewhere too.

516
00:44:25,350 --> 00:44:31,148
We're not just stretching and twisting
this taffy for no reason.

517
00:44:32,024 --> 00:44:35,986
We're letting air into it.

518
00:44:36,069 --> 00:44:41,283
If you keep flattening and folding
the taffy over and over,

519
00:44:41,867 --> 00:44:45,412
it forms air bubbles in the center.

520
00:44:45,996 --> 00:44:50,834
The air bubbles
make it sweeter and crumblier.

521
00:44:50,918 --> 00:44:53,754
That's how we make better taffy.

522
00:44:55,964 --> 00:44:57,966
It's the same for people.

523
00:44:58,550 --> 00:45:01,470
Not having any flaws
isn't always a good thing.

524
00:45:03,806 --> 00:45:07,851
If you end up having a few holes
for whatever reason,

525
00:45:08,435 --> 00:45:12,272
you'll find that your tough life
becomes sweeter and crumblier.

526
00:45:12,773 --> 00:45:15,943
And it'll make you a better person.

527
00:45:17,611 --> 00:45:21,114
So it's okay to be a little embarrassed.

528
00:45:21,615 --> 00:45:25,244
It's completely fine for a person
to be embarrassed once in a while.

529
00:45:36,797 --> 00:45:38,549
I'm sorry.

530
00:45:42,261 --> 00:45:43,637
I'm so sorry.

531
00:45:45,138 --> 00:45:48,433
I thought you were a lady,
but you're just a baby.

532
00:45:48,934 --> 00:45:50,435
Look at you.

533
00:46:17,296 --> 00:46:18,630
Hello.

534
00:46:26,305 --> 00:46:27,264
Tae-ha, that punk…

535
00:46:29,725 --> 00:46:32,811
He was no ordinary kid.

536
00:46:33,520 --> 00:46:35,939
In just six months of training with me,

537
00:46:36,023 --> 00:46:40,444
he swept the city, province,
and national competitions.

538
00:46:41,069 --> 00:46:46,325
In no time, he became a national athlete
and trained at Taereung.

539
00:46:49,369 --> 00:46:52,623
But then, the old lady became unwell.

540
00:46:54,291 --> 00:46:55,417
His grandmother?

541
00:46:56,084 --> 00:46:59,212
Yes. Though she's technically
not his real grandmother.

542
00:47:01,340 --> 00:47:03,300
She's not his real grandmother?

543
00:47:03,383 --> 00:47:06,887
With nowhere to go, Tae-ha's mom
stumbled into our village with a newborn,

544
00:47:06,970 --> 00:47:09,806
then died after staying at
Lady Go's house for a while.

545
00:47:10,599 --> 00:47:12,768
So the old lady raised Tae-ha.

546
00:47:15,479 --> 00:47:18,982
I thought they were family.

547
00:47:19,483 --> 00:47:21,109
They are family.

548
00:47:21,193 --> 00:47:23,946
Do they have to be blood-related
to be family?

549
00:47:24,029 --> 00:47:26,156
That's it! My Tae-ha, you're doing great.

550
00:47:26,239 --> 00:47:27,908
Tae-ha, don't get worked up.

551
00:47:30,285 --> 00:47:31,286
Stop!

552
00:47:31,912 --> 00:47:35,290
She raised him with more care
than she would her own grandchildren.

553
00:47:35,374 --> 00:47:37,292
-Wasn't I great?
-Yes!

554
00:47:37,376 --> 00:47:40,212
The old lady was so warm,
showering him with endless love.

555
00:47:40,295 --> 00:47:41,922
My baby, you did great.

556
00:47:42,005 --> 00:47:45,592
Until then, there were no shadows
in Tae-ha's life.

557
00:48:02,484 --> 00:48:05,696
TAE-HA, GRANDMA COLLAPSED
COME TO BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

558
00:48:07,906 --> 00:48:12,202
Perhaps that's why
he wanted to save her no matter what.

559
00:48:14,371 --> 00:48:17,207
But the surgery and medication
cost nearly a hundred million,

560
00:48:17,708 --> 00:48:19,960
and Tae-ha was only 20 years old.

561
00:48:21,169 --> 00:48:23,046
Where could he get that kind of money?

562
00:48:23,797 --> 00:48:26,466
He couldn't afford it
with his training camp allowance,

563
00:48:26,550 --> 00:48:29,136
and his signing bonus
from the semipro team wasn't much.

564
00:48:30,429 --> 00:48:31,847
And that's when

565
00:48:32,431 --> 00:48:36,601
this gang called Geukrakpa
reached out to him.

566
00:48:46,028 --> 00:48:48,030
His grandma survived,

567
00:48:48,530 --> 00:48:51,992
but when she found out
how Tae-ha had saved her,

568
00:48:52,951 --> 00:48:56,121
she soon started to slip away.

569
00:48:57,581 --> 00:48:59,541
She couldn't go on living

570
00:49:00,417 --> 00:49:02,377
without erasing the memory of that.

571
00:49:14,473 --> 00:49:18,643
After Tae-ha became a gangster,
he lived like a machine.

572
00:49:18,727 --> 00:49:21,271
Beating people up
and breaking things on command.

573
00:49:32,157 --> 00:49:34,534
He lived like that for 14 years,

574
00:49:34,618 --> 00:49:37,370
afraid that he might have regrets
if he ever looked back.

575
00:50:44,729 --> 00:50:47,691
But he's always been too kind by nature.

576
00:50:48,650 --> 00:50:50,986
No matter how much
he tried to live like a machine,

577
00:50:52,028 --> 00:50:54,114
he couldn't help
but feel sick to his stomach.

578
00:51:07,002 --> 00:51:07,878
That's why

579
00:51:09,754 --> 00:51:11,089
he came back.

580
00:51:16,845 --> 00:51:18,471
Tae-ha's heart

581
00:51:19,556 --> 00:51:20,599
is deeply wounded.

582
00:51:22,058 --> 00:51:23,935
A wound that will never heal

583
00:51:24,019 --> 00:51:26,563
and that will never fade.

584
00:51:27,772 --> 00:51:29,274
I don't know about anyone else,

585
00:51:29,357 --> 00:51:30,692
but you…

586
00:51:31,985 --> 00:51:36,198
I just hope you won't make
that wound any worse.

587
00:51:46,917 --> 00:51:49,252
-Excuse me.
-Sure.

588
00:51:50,545 --> 00:51:51,630
Hello.

589
00:51:52,422 --> 00:51:54,090
Yes, this is Hong's Boxing Gym.

590
00:51:55,592 --> 00:51:56,509
Sorry?

591
00:51:57,469 --> 00:51:58,595
Tae-ha?

592
00:52:00,263 --> 00:52:02,432
You're honestly blaming me for this?

593
00:52:02,515 --> 00:52:05,518
I told you that bastard
broke my side mirror and just ran off!

594
00:52:05,602 --> 00:52:06,436
Come on now.

595
00:52:06,519 --> 00:52:09,522
He said he had an emergency
and left his contact information.

596
00:52:09,606 --> 00:52:11,066
Did he not?

597
00:52:11,149 --> 00:52:13,318
Then why didn't he call me
after he was done?

598
00:52:13,401 --> 00:52:15,779
I had to call him and drag him out here!

599
00:52:15,862 --> 00:52:17,697
How is this not a hit-and-run?

600
00:52:18,281 --> 00:52:20,116
You didn't have to mess up his face.

601
00:52:20,700 --> 00:52:23,286
Violence can never be justified!

602
00:52:23,370 --> 00:52:25,247
-What the hell happened?
-There you are.

603
00:52:27,207 --> 00:52:28,250
Go Eun-sae.

604
00:52:29,459 --> 00:52:30,585
Did you get beat up?

605
00:52:31,169 --> 00:52:32,587
No, I…

606
00:52:36,341 --> 00:52:37,801
Oh, dear God.

607
00:52:38,510 --> 00:52:41,346
-Where is your family burial ground?
-What now?

608
00:52:41,930 --> 00:52:43,181
Bow in that direction. Now.

609
00:52:44,474 --> 00:52:46,559
If he's held back any less,

610
00:52:47,686 --> 00:52:50,230
you'd be joining your ancestors by now.

611
00:52:50,313 --> 00:52:51,731
What the hell are you on about?

612
00:52:52,315 --> 00:52:53,650
I'm his guardian.

613
00:52:53,733 --> 00:52:58,530
I'll replace that side mirror
with the fanciest one out there.

614
00:52:58,613 --> 00:52:59,656
Talk it out with me.

615
00:53:00,365 --> 00:53:02,367
You're laughing? You think this is funny?

616
00:53:02,450 --> 00:53:04,077
-You wanna go?
-Let's go talk.

617
00:53:04,160 --> 00:53:05,453
Do-yeop, you can't hit him.

618
00:53:31,229 --> 00:53:34,691
I thought you were a good boxer.
A former gangster.

619
00:53:34,774 --> 00:53:37,485
Couldn't you have just knocked him out
with a few punches?

620
00:53:40,572 --> 00:53:42,615
It wouldn't have taken a few.

621
00:53:43,116 --> 00:53:43,950
Just one.

622
00:53:44,034 --> 00:53:44,993
Exactly.

623
00:53:46,077 --> 00:53:48,455
So why did you let him
beat you up like this?

624
00:53:50,957 --> 00:53:52,208
I didn't get beat up.

625
00:53:52,959 --> 00:53:54,419
I was blocking, and…

626
00:54:03,803 --> 00:54:04,763
I promised you.

627
00:54:06,181 --> 00:54:07,015
What?

628
00:54:12,103 --> 00:54:14,397
I won't ever use my fists
outside the ring anymore.

629
00:54:15,815 --> 00:54:16,858
I promise.

630
00:54:29,496 --> 00:54:30,330
That's why…

631
00:54:32,832 --> 00:54:34,626
you just let him beat you up?

632
00:54:38,630 --> 00:54:39,672
Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

633
00:54:40,423 --> 00:54:41,383
Are you stupid?

634
00:54:42,550 --> 00:54:46,471
Why would you stand there and take it
when you did nothing wrong?

635
00:54:46,554 --> 00:54:48,264
You hit back in situations like this.

636
00:54:48,348 --> 00:54:49,849
You should have hit him back.

637
00:55:11,621 --> 00:55:12,831
What should I do with you?

638
00:55:17,669 --> 00:55:19,629
This must be why I liked you.

639
00:55:20,839 --> 00:55:22,549
Gangster or not,

640
00:55:23,591 --> 00:55:25,677
that must be why.

641
00:55:28,972 --> 00:55:30,265
I'm sorry.

642
00:55:33,601 --> 00:55:36,104
I'm sorry for not remembering you
and making you upset.

643
00:56:17,103 --> 00:56:18,771
OUR STICKY LOVE

644
00:57:05,401 --> 00:57:09,364
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

